    "readings": "The pale front parapet spans roughly 31–32 m in two dated images. A red cover behind it tapers at the front and terminates against a higher rear roof. A narrow pale strip on the eastern part of the higher roof is conspicuous in both 2021 and 2025. The southern rim and central cover move several metres between image dates because of the non-nadir view and registration. Coarse map polygon endpoints cannot fix the wall-to-roof overhang.",
    "height": "Ridge and stage heights and the back of the parapet remain approximate. The north-side roofs beyond the polygon have separate footprint records. Three rays to the far-right block of the 1934 photograph miss the published auditorium. Its connection to the 1934 hall is unresolved."
  }
